  "goodToKnow": "Die Chemikalie, mostly used in the plural Chemikalien, is a chemical: gefährliche Chemikalien, Haushaltschemikalien. Germany's chemical industry is huge, led by BASF in Ludwigshafen, Bayer and Evonik. The ch in Chemie is pronounced like in ich in the north (çe-MEE) and like k in the south and Austria (ke-MEE), and both are correct. The EU regulates chemicals under REACH, based in Helsinki. Plural: die Chemikalien."
